io_uring/kbuf: check if target buffer list is still legacy on recycle

jira KERNEL-1731
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-687.56.1.el9_8
commit-author Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
commit c2c185be5c85d37215397c8e8781abf0a69bec1f
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-687.56.1.el9_8/c2c185be.failed

There's a gap between when the buffer was grabbed and when it
potentially gets recycled, where if the list is empty, someone could've
upgraded it to a ring provided type. This can happen if the request
is forced via io-wq. The legacy recycling is missing checking if the
buffer_list still exists, and if it's of the correct type. Add those
checks.

	Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Fixes: c7fb19428d67 ("io_uring: add support for ring mapped supplied buffers")
	Reported-by: Keenan Dong <keenanat2000@gmail.com>
	Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
(cherry picked from commit c2c185be5c85d37215397c8e8781abf0a69bec1f)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	io_uring/kbuf.c
diff --cc io_uring/kbuf.c
index 919d2d22d61f,e7f444953dfb..000000000000
--- a/io_uring/kbuf.c
+++ b/io_uring/kbuf.c
@@@ -62,9 -111,18 +62,24 @@@ bool io_kbuf_recycle_legacy(struct io_k
  
  	buf = req->kbuf;
  	bl = io_buffer_get_list(ctx, buf->bgid);
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	list_add(&buf->list, &bl->buf_list);
 +	req->flags &= ~REQ_F_BUFFER_SELECTED;
 +	req->buf_index = buf->bgid;
++=======
+ 	/*
+ 	 * If the buffer list was upgraded to a ring-based one, or removed,
+ 	 * while the request was in-flight in io-wq, drop it.
+ 	 */
+ 	if (bl && !(bl->flags & IOBL_BUF_RING)) {
+ 		list_add(&buf->list, &bl->buf_list);
+ 		bl->nbufs++;
+ 	} else {
+ 		kfree(buf);
+ 	}
+ 	req->flags &= ~REQ_F_BUFFER_SELECTED;
+ 	req->kbuf = NULL;
++>>>>>>> c2c185be5c85 (io_uring/kbuf: check if target buffer list is still legacy on recycle)
  
  	io_ring_submit_unlock(ctx, issue_flags);
  	return true;
* Unmerged path io_uring/kbuf.c
